        "original_id": "a775ade2-2612-5834-bf56-2f28861f3062",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Barranca de Yaco, Barranca Yaco, Villa Tulumba, Sinsacate, Córdoba, Argentina\n- Systems: Inca road system, camino real\n- Organizations: Viceroyalty of the Río de la Plata\n- Concepts: place-name etymology, geography\n\nFacts:\n- The Inca road system was about 24,800 miles long.\n- Barranca de Yaco, also called Barranca Yaco, is a geographical feature along the ancient camino real of the Viceroyalty of the Río de la Plata.\n- Barranca de Yaco is located between Villa Tulumba and Sinsacate in Córdoba Province, Argentina.\n- The name Barranca de Yaco derives from the Spanish word \"barranca,\" meaning gully, and the Quechua word \"yaku,\" meaning water.",
